WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.674
Joy woke up to the smell of pancakes.

2
00:00:06.675 --> 00:00:10.020
"Mom is making pancakes?" she thought.

3
00:00:10.021 --> 00:00:12.043
That was unusual.

4
00:00:12.044 --> 00:00:14.949
Joy rushed downstairs.

5
00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:17.695
"Grandpa!" she cried.

6
00:00:17.696 --> 00:00:21.712
Grandpa was in front of the stove, flipping pancakes.

7
00:00:21.713 --> 00:00:25.021
"Who wants pancakes?" he asked.

8
00:00:25.022 --> 00:00:28.491
Joy gave her grandfather a huge hug.

9
00:00:28.492 --> 00:00:30.611
"When did you get back?"

10
00:00:30.612 --> 00:00:31.852
"Early this morning.

11
00:00:31.853 --> 00:00:36.428
Your dad and I woke up at sunrise and drove straight here," he said.

12
00:00:36.429 --> 00:00:39.724
"I heard you were up late, finishing schoolwork."

13
00:00:39.725 --> 00:00:45.025
Joy grinned. "I was. But I finished my leaders project.

14
00:00:45.026 --> 00:00:49.017
So I'm ready for pancakes and ready to play in the snow!"

15
00:00:49.018 --> 00:00:52.382
Just then Katie bounced into the kitchen.

16
00:00:52.383 --> 00:00:57.335
At the same time, Dad came in the backdoor, carrying firewood.

17
00:00:57.336 --> 00:00:59.561
Mom followed him.

18
00:00:59.562 --> 00:01:04.354
"Dad! Grandpa!" Katie cried, surprised.

19
00:01:04.355 --> 00:01:08.474
"I can't wait to hear all about your weekend," Dad said.

20
00:01:08.475 --> 00:01:13.680
He gave Katie's ponytail a playful tug.

21
00:01:13.681 --> 00:01:18.279
"Isn't it nice that we're all home together again?" Mom said.

22
00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:22.867
Grandpa set a huge stack of pancakes on the table.

23
00:01:22.868 --> 00:01:30.717
"And isn't it nice that Grandpa is back to cook breakfast for us?" Katie replied. Mom laughed.

24
00:01:30.718 --> 00:01:34.796
"So what did we miss while we were away?" Grandpa asked.

25
00:01:34.797 --> 00:01:36.735
He winked at Mom.

26
00:01:36.736 --> 00:01:40.657
"Besides cold cereal and burnt brownies?"

27
00:01:40.658 --> 00:01:46.357
"Well, first of all, it was freezing outside," Katie began.

28
00:01:46.358 --> 00:01:50.575
"And we thought we had an egg and chicken thief!" Joy added.

29
00:01:50.576 --> 00:01:54.637
"But really some chickens were escaping through a hole in the fence!

30
00:01:54.638 --> 00:02:00.029
And they were laying eggs in your burn pile, Grandpa," Katie said.

31
00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:03.552
"Wow!" said Grandpa, surprised.

32
00:02:03.553 --> 00:02:07.018
"I'm glad there wasn't a real thief!" said Dad.

33
00:02:07.019 --> 00:02:14.906
"Then Joy fixed the hole in the fence all by herself," Katie said with her mouth full of pancakes.

34
00:02:14.907 --> 00:02:17.900
"Wonderful!" said Grandpa.

35
00:02:17.901 --> 00:02:23.447
"And tomorrow at school we're finally giving our reports on leaders," said Joy.

36
00:02:23.448 --> 00:02:27.507
"Who did you end up choosing, Joy?" Grandpa asked.

37
00:02:27.508 --> 00:02:30.449
"Harriet Tubman," Joy said.

38
00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:33.871
"She spent her whole life working for something

39
00:02:33.872 --> 00:02:36.194
important: getting slaves to

40
00:02:36.195 --> 00:02:38.884
freedom." "Good choice," said

41
00:02:38.885 --> 00:02:44.842
Dad. "Thanks." Joy poured maple syrup on her pancakes, thinking for a

42
00:02:44.843 --> 00:02:49.185
minute. Would she ever be a great leader like Harriet

43
00:02:49.186 --> 00:02:51.848
Tubman? "Dad," Joy said

44
00:02:51.849 --> 00:02:55.798
slowly. "When you were a kid, what did you want to be when you grew

45
00:02:55.799 --> 00:03:00.838
up?" Dad smiled. "I wanted to work in a park, taking care of

46
00:03:00.839 --> 00:03:06.075
trees." "Now you take care of trees by helping people recycle!" Katie

47
00:03:06.076 --> 00:03:09.737
said. Dad laughed. "I guess I

48
00:03:09.738 --> 00:03:12.967
do." "What about you, Grandpa?" asked

49
00:03:12.968 --> 00:03:17.544
Katie. Grandpa had been a mailman in Willow Creek for thirty

50
00:03:17.545 --> 00:03:23.033
years. "I knew I wanted to be a mailman since I was nine years old," Grandpa

51
00:03:23.034 --> 00:03:27.934
said. "I loved seeing people smile when they got a special letter or

52
00:03:27.935 --> 00:03:32.214
package." "I always wanted to be a librarian," Mom chimed

53
00:03:32.215 --> 00:03:34.322
in. "What about you

54
00:03:34.323 --> 00:03:38.879
girls?" "I'm going to be the mayor of Willow Creek!" Katie

55
00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:42.251
announced. Dad laughed. "That's perfect for

56
00:03:42.252 --> 00:03:45.146
you." Joy grinned from ear to

57
00:03:45.147 --> 00:03:48.221
ear. "I want to be a vet," she

58
00:03:48.222 --> 00:03:51.917
said. "Those are great jobs," Grandpa

59
00:03:51.918 --> 00:03:55.022
said. "They're about helping others, just like leaders

60
00:03:55.023 --> 00:03:57.292
do. And like sisters do

61
00:03:57.293 --> 00:04:00.276
too." The twins smiled at each

62
00:04:00.277 --> 00:04:02.765
other. "So, sister," Katie

63
00:04:02.766 --> 00:04:05.590
said. "Are you done with your pancakes

64
00:04:05.591 --> 00:04:09.078
yet?" "Yep. I'm done," Joy told her

65
00:04:09.079 --> 00:04:12.890
twin. "Time to go play in the

66
00:04:12.891 --> 00:04:15.408
snow!" Katie was already by the

67
00:04:15.409 --> 00:04:19.663
door. "Catch!" she said, tossing Joy's boots at

68
00:04:19.664 --> 00:04:22.634
her. Joy laughed as she caught the

69
00:04:22.635 --> 00:04:26.415
boots. Sometimes she wished she had an older

70
00:04:26.416 --> 00:04:29.994
sister. Other times she wished she had a younger

71
00:04:29.995 --> 00:04:35.577
sister. But today she was glad that she and Katie were

72
00:04:35.578 --> 00:04:39.582
twins. "Isn't it fun being a twin sister?" Joy

73
00:04:39.583 --> 00:04:42.471
asked. "Yes," answered

74
00:04:42.472 --> 00:04:47.062
Katie. "Sometimes it's even fun being your twin

75
00:04:47.063 --> 00:04:54.055
sister!" Then the Willow Creek twins raced out into the snow

76
00:04:54.056 --> 00:05:27.584
together.

